From 10655ecd51c3204d7603b3ca849a407c9eaa1db0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shahrokh <design@cariblanco.best>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 21:45:18 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 06/12] system-prompt prefill cache works with --layer-split
 (one session file per stage) and with host-RAM K/V

The F5 gate only enabled the cache with stages.empty() && use_mtp (single GPU). This removes that restriction and makes the variant a per-stage artifact: one byte-for-byte session file per stage plus a joint sidecar (same carve the conversation disk tier writes), so the cache works multi-GPU and under --batch. The sidecar is v2 (stage count + total bytes; v1 still read) with a checksum; the scan never deletes (a broken sidecar, a foreign identity, an orphan file and an incomplete variant are counted and kept), and only the GC removes, oldest first.

load() reads and validates EVERY stage file before replacing the output image, so a missing, foreign or corrupt stage refuses the whole variant with no partial state. The streamed store takes one (K/V-empty meta, sources) pair per stage, stage 0 first, the draft layer's K/V riding with the last stage; every source's read carries its own device because the callbacks run while the file is written.

Host-RAM (streaming) K/V: the source is the authoritative host pool (conversation_cache.hpp), never the replaceable VRAM slots, and the restore path (conversation_snapshot_restore per stage) calls refill_residency, which resets the streaming window (kv_stream_reset) or refills the draft ring (kv_ring_restore) - the PR #1269 lesson, so no stale slots are read after a multi-stage restore.

conversation_snapshot_sources gains the draft==nullptr overload so a stage without the draft's K/V can be captured. conversation_prompt_cache_test: 52 -> 100 checks (2-stage round-trip byte for byte, stage mismatch refused clean, two variants coexisting, host-pool streamed round-trip, inert without flags). conversation_spill_test stays at 102.
